# Martins Distribution Invoice Processing Application

## Overview

The Martins Distribution Invoice Processing Application (MDIP) is a Windows desktop application that extracts information from Martin's Distribution invoice PDF files, validates the invoice information according to client-specific requirements, and exports the resulting invoice data as CSV files for client submission.

The application is designed to reduce manual invoice-entry work, provide validation before processing, and maintain a small local processing history for recently completed batches.

## Features

- Extracts invoice information and line-item data from Martin's Distribution PDF invoices.
- Extracts invoice metadata including:
  - Customer number
  - Customer name
  - Customer purchase order
  - Delivery date
  - Invoice number
  - Invoice total
- Exports processed invoices as client-compatible CSV files.
- Supports multiple client locations:
  - Taco Bamba
  - Velvet Taco North Hills
  - Velvet Taco Southend
  - Velvet Taco Park Rd
- Applies client-specific Customer PO validation rules before processing.
- Allows approved exceptions for office-created or system-created second-delivery invoices when permitted by the validation rules.
- Includes invoice delivery dates in validation and processing-history views.
- Detects invoice numbers that were processed in one of the two most recent successful batches and provides a duplicate-processing warning before processing.
- Maintains a local history of the two most recent successful processing batches.
- Records processing information such as user, machine, batch, invoice, client, output file, and approved PO exceptions.
- Provides a processing progress interface and opens the resulting file in Windows Explorer after successful processing.
- Supports drag-and-drop invoice selection when `tkinterdnd2` is available.
- Uses local application data for configuration, history, and logging.

## Project Structure

The project uses `MDIP.py` as the application entry point.

```text
pdf_reader/
├── MDIP.py
├── Martins-Distribution_RGB.ico
├── Readme
├── requirements.txt
└── src/
    ├── main.py
    ├── models.py
    ├── validation.py
    ├── logging_config.py
    └── services/
        └── history_manager.py
        └── explorer_manager.py
```

## Configuration

On first launch, the application asks the user to select:

1. The folder containing invoice PDFs.
2. The folder where processed CSV files should be saved.

The configuration is stored locally in:

```text
%LOCALAPPDATA%\\MD Invoice Processor\\config.json
```

## Processing Workflow

The normal processing workflow is:

```text
Select invoice PDF(s)
        ↓
Scan and extract invoice information
        ↓
Validate client and Customer PO requirements
        ↓
Review exceptions when applicable
        ↓
Check recent invoice history for duplicates
        ↓
Process invoice(s)
        ↓
Export CSV file(s)
        ↓
Record successful batch in history
        ↓
Reveal the output file in Windows Explorer
```

A batch is only added to processing history when all selected invoices complete successfully.

## Local Application Data

MDIP stores application data under:

```text
%LOCALAPPDATA%\\MD Invoice Processor
```

The directory contains the following:

```text
config.json
history.json
logs\\app.log
```

`history.json` contains the two most recent successfully completed processing batches.

The local log is intended to provide a fallback record of application activity. A network log location may also be configured.

## Requirements

The application is developed for Windows and uses Python.

Install the project dependencies with:

```cmd
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

PyInstaller is required only when creating the standalone executable:

```cmd
pip install pyinstaller
```

## Creating the Standalone Executable

Run the following command from the project root directory:

```cmd
pyinstaller ^
    --onefile ^
    --windowed ^
    --clean ^
    --noconfirm ^
    --icon="Martins-Distribution_RGB.ico" ^
    --collect-all tkinterdnd2 ^
    --collect-all pydantic_core ^
    --collect-all pymupdf ^
    --add-data "Martins-Distribution_RGB.ico;." ^
    MDIP.py
```

After the build completes, the standalone executable will be located in:

```text
dist\\MDIP.exe
```

`MDIP.exe` packages the Python application and its required Python dependencies into a single Windows executable so the application can be distributed to other Windows devices without requiring the user to manually install the Python project dependencies.

## Development

For normal development, run the application from the project root:

```cmd
python MDIP.py
```

The application entry point is:

```text
MDIP.py
```

The reusable processing and business logic is contained in the `src` package.

## Notes

- Keep `MDIP.py` in the project root when running the application or building the executable.
- Keep the Martins Distribution icon file available to PyInstaller during the build.
- Only successfully completed batches are recorded in processing history.
- Duplicate invoice detection is intended as a warning and confirmation step rather than a hard block.
- The application does not modify the source invoice PDF when an exception is approved. The exception affects the value written to the outbound CSV.
